SUMMARY:Queer History of Durham Tour: Downtown Edition
DESCRIPTION:During Durham’s Pride Week\, the Durham LGBTQ Center\, Preservation Durham\, the Pauli Murray Center for History and Social Justice\, and the Museum of Durham History are excited to host the Queer History of Durham Tour: Downtown Edition. \nThis is a walking tour\, with about a mile worth of walking in Durham’s downtown social district. Registration is free\, with an optional donation. \nMeeting spot: Museum of Durham History (500 W. Main St.) \nFriday\, October 2nd (Three different time slots) \n3:00pm-4:00pm \n4:30pm-5:30pm \n6:00pm-7:00pm \n 
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/queer-history-of-durham-tour-downtown-edition/
LOCATION:Museum of Durham History\, 500 W. Main St.\, Durham\, NC\, 27701\, United States
CATEGORIES:Pride
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Screenshot-2026-09-09-at-4.37.02-PM.jpg
GEO:35.9982983;-78.9049764
