SUMMARY:Durham Square Dance
DESCRIPTION:The Durham Square Dance is a community-driven group that supports artistic expression via old time music and collective movement.\nNew and experienced dancers are welcome. You don’t need to bring a partner. There’s a caller who teaches every move and guides you through the wild adventure. A live band plays rippin’ tunes to drive the energy. All in all\, your face should hurt by the end from smiling. \nFamily Square Dance\, 5-6pm. Slower-paced\, for kiddos and their adults.\nBig Square Dance\, 7-9pm. Faster-paced\, for anyone out for an adventure. Expect some easy moves\, some silly moves\, and a good time for anyone. \nCalling by Nancy Mamlin for both dances. \nYou can choose to pay for a $10\, $15\, or $20 ticket based on your personal financial situation and ability to support the local arts scene. Kids under 12 are free! One ticket will get you into both dances.
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/durham-square-dance/
LOCATION:The Pinhook\, 117 W Main St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701\, United States
CATEGORIES:Dance,Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Oct-4-Square-Dance-Website-Social.jpg
